WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.240
CLINT: Oh shoot, where your lips at?

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.600
*laughing*

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:04.520
Whoa!

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.640
Guys, I don't know if you know;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.420
maybe some of you know, but most of you probably don't...

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.120
*slurp*

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.660
I love drawing. I... loooove drawing.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.720
I loved drawing since I was like three years old,

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.320
and off and on I've been, like, practicing,

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.180
you know what I'm sayin'?

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.260
As a kid, I always love, like,

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.880
how to draw tanks, how to draw airplanes,

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.300
and how to draw wrestlers, and how to draw all the good stuff, right?

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.920
Over time I was trying to figure out different ways to draw.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.300
You can use watercolor, you can use pencil, you can use a pen -

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.920
and you can do it in all these different styles,

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.720
and I came across this one style -

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:34.920
it's like a contour drawing,

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.400
where you can't pick up your pen from what you're drawing,

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:37.720
AND it's blind.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.580
You can't look at what you're drawing.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:43.200
You have 30 seconds to draw your best friend's face.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.420
Alright, who do ya wanna start with?

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:45.700
NICK: Let's go up and see Sam.
CLINT: Okay.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.080
NICK: Hey Sayyum!
SAM: 'Suuup?

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.300
SAM: Here lemme give you, like, a little nice - easy, classic portrait.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.040
CLINT: Yeah, that's perfect.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.840
It's like the pano - the squish pano, right?

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.060
You have the randomness of, like, I dunno what I'm gonna get,

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.760
but you might get some gold.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:58.720
Alright, you ready?

00:00:58.720 --> 00:00:59.540
Here we go!

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.680
Once you do that, you elevate it, right?

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:04.700
You take it to the next level,

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.840
And you shade it, like you shade it really well.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.920
And it looks... and it just looks beautiful.
NICK: *laughs*

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.020
CLINT: Schweet.
SAM: Whooaa!

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.340
There's some crazy stuff in here.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:14.460
This is Brett-son.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.060
There's another son right here.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:16.960
There's Cliff again.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.320
SAM: What do you do to practice drawing? Wow, that was sweet.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.840
Do it, do it, do it, do it, do it?

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.080
CLINT: Yeah. Inktober is a thing where you, like,

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.020
draw something in ink every single day,

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:26.720
That helped a lot, actually, 'cause like,

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:28.840
at first I was like, super careful about what I did,

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:31.200
and then over the course of the month, I kind of developed a style,

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.080
like a sketchy style, like, this is kind of

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:35.260
the style - like, what came of this style.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.320
It's kind of sketchy and not really precise,

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.020
because with a pen, you just wanna kinda like -

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:40.300
just go with it, you know?

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.140
JAKE: What're you guys doin'?

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:43.080
CLINT: This is Sam.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.160
JAKE: *chuckles* That's actually - that's actually -

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:46.740
It resembles him!

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.900
I like the rule that you can't remove the pen from the paper.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.600
That really, I think, gives it a whole new level of -

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:53.980
CLINT: It's the bonus challenge.
JAKE: Yeah.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.080
We should go around, we should draw everyone,

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.220
and then freaking frame them, dude, just frame 'em up!

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.520
Imma grab a pen, and I'm just gonna - just draw everyone.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.680
30 seconds, can't look at it, can't pick up my pen -

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:04.740
Let's try it!

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:10.300
*laughing*
Dude, this one - this one's the best one!

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.460
JAKE: I've never had my portrait drawn before.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.760
CLINT: You're about to be horribly disappointed!
*both laughing*

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.920
CLINT: Oh shoot, where your lips at?

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.160
Maybe that's where they are...

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.200
You kinda have to start - yeah, in the center,

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.900
'cause then you know, like, where you're at,

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.860
and kinda go from there.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:25.600
NIKO: It's like a perfect photograph! *chuckles*

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.260
*muffled laughter*

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.000
CLINT: That one! That one, dude!

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.820
JAKE: That is a freakin' masterpiece!

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:33.340
WREN: 'Kay, you guys are reacting...

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:36.900
*laughter* Whooaa!

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.460
JAKE: These are starting to become incredible.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:39.740
NICK: You're not allowed to see it.
WREN: I know, I know.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:43.860
CHRISTIAN: I want to see mine.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:46.820
(Oh no...)

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.320
CLINT: Dude, that's like, some straight-up Planet of the Apes!

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.320
ADRIAN: Oh yeah, I can see the resemblance.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:54.340
Alright, here we go...

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.420
WREN: I don't know anything about this soda,

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.840
other than what Adrian's told me about it.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.220
And I'm really intrigued. I like sour things,

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.280
but this sounds like it might be too intense.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.440
Yeah, so ever since Adrian broke his collar bone, he's been unable to drive.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.380
Since we live within a couple of miles from each other,

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.580
I've just been driving him to work every day.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.760
Which is not a problem, but he, you know, has wanted to show his appreciation,

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.680
by giving me the world's most sour soda, apparently.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:17.960
JAKE: I have no idea what that means.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.060
WREN: Sour soda!

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:20.520
ADRIAN: I thought you would like how the bottle looked,

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.180
I mean, I thought the bottle looked pretty badass.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.120
WREN: Wait, wasn't this Niko's?

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.020
ADRIAN: No that's mine.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.680
WREN: Excuse me?!
*laughter*

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.320
Excuse me?! That was almost too easy!

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.500
ADRIAN: That is cruel, Wren! That is cruel.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:32.580
JAKE: Dude...

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.400
ADRIAN: ...do one arm, I guess, I dunno.
JAKE: Wait -

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.300
We need to get - we need to get somebody else's opinion on this.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.480
NIKO: What's the rule?

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.800
JAKE: The rule is, if you're in the game, you're in the game.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.340
NIKO: And if he leaves, it exponentially goes up.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.460
JAKE: Yeah, and if he doesn't do them right now,

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.380
for the full extent of his injury...

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.840
NIKO: Well you could always pull a Jake and just never fulfill his debt.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:55.000
JAKE: Hey hey hey hey hey - alright maybe I shouldn't have asked you.

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:56.480
NIKO: Can you do a one-handed push-up?

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:58.560
ADRIAN: ... yeah.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.040
ADRIAN: Wait wait wait wait wait wait wait - **** that.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.920
Wait, I did a hundred push-ups like a month ago.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.860
["$100 for 100 Push Up Challenge"]
*cheering*

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:16.740
CARMICHAEL: Adrian, you won yourself a Game of Life credit!

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.780
ADRIAN: I got ONE credit!

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.900
ADRIAN: ... right? That counts as a credit!

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.600
That counts as a credit, right?

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:26.980
Hell yeah, I'm turning in my credit! I got a broken clavicle!

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.760
Wanted to do 10 push-ups (!)

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:32.080
WREN: But now I guess the question is, like,

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.060
*should* you have to spend the credit?

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:39.140
(dude) (absolutely!)
ADRIAN: This is WHY you do the hundred push-ups!

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.540
For times like this!

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:44.000
NIKO: See, everybody? Long-term investments pay off!

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.300
*laughing*

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.500
WREN: What?!

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.520
CLINT: Shading - We got this janky outline,

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.560
and I'm gonna try and make it look 3D.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.660
and try to render it, almost, right?

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.420
Essentially anything that's white is coming towards the camera,

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.720
anything that's black is going away from camera,

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.740
and I'll probably just choose a general light source.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:05.640
I'll just start.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:08.340
Imma just do, like, the lightest values first,

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:11.280
and I'm gonna shade everything at a very light value

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.980
as a test to see: is this where I want my lighting to come from?

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.000
I'm gonna use this - paper towel -

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.820
to smudge it and smear it so it's like super smooth,

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.260
and it looks just like baby smooth, you know what I mean?

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:23.400
They sell little rolls of paper,

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:24.600
specifically for this

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.200
It looks like a pencil but it's made of paper.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.600
I got, like, a general shadow on this thing,

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.180
and I'm gonna start making the values

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.340
darker and darker and darker and darker...

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:35.920
So that's the first one - it's about 5 minutes.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:38.420
NICK: Niiice.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:40.420
ADRIAN: Hey Wren, are you gonna drink that drink?

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:42.780
I wanna see you chug it, for - for doing that to me!

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:43.840
He better chug it.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.620
WREN: I loved Warheads, back when I was in 4th grade.

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.620
Oh my god, it's literally black!
ADRIAN: Oh yeah.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.300
WREN: It smells like - *coughing*

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.840
It smells like regular Coke, but then after like a moment,

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:55.520
it hit my lungs, and then, like, seized it up.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:56.240
*coughing*

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:58.580
GABE: Oh yeah.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:01.500
I used to eat Warheads so much that it would make my tongue bleed.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.000
And I'd still eat more.
WREN: Dude, get that - the raw tongue?

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.000
GABE: Yeah.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.280
JAKE: Just drink the soda, man!

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:07.460
Stop stallin'.

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:08.760
WREN: I just wanna try it!

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:09.720
JAKE: Just drink the soda.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:10.640
WREN: Okay, a little bit more...

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:13.020
JAKE: I mean, not like stop Stal- Stalin has already been stopped,

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:14.900
I mean, like, stop *stalling*.

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:16.740
[johnyboz] *laughing*

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:18.360
WREN: Alright, I'm gonna try it.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.000
(It's not that bad)
WREN: It's not even sour.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.240
ADRIAN: Yeah, that's what I thought.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.700
But it's not like - yeah look at Wren - it's drinkable still...

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:31.140
NICK: Is it worse than coin juice?

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:33.360
["Drinking 2000 year-old Coin Juice"] Whooaa! Augghh!

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:35.840
*sputtering*

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:37.840
NICK: Ewwwww!

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:39.360
WREN: Nothing's worse than coin juice, man...

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.820
JAKE: Alright, well that was interesting. Thanks for sharin'.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:44.040
WREN: This was supposed to be a much cooler segment.

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:46.500
NICK: Chug chug chug...!
WREN: No man.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.160
CLINT: Time to reveal the final shots here.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:49.420
Some of these turned out,

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:51.340
looking like really funny versions of all y'all,

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:54.460
and some of these turned out looking like real ugly versions of you guys,

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:56.700
and some just turned out not looking like you guys.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:58.160
Alright here we go - Sam, that's you!

00:06:58.540 --> 00:06:59.700
*chuckling*

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:01.300
SAM: Dude that's art!

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:02.500
CHRISTIAN: Oh my god!

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.320
SAM: It's like Picasso.
NIKO: I can recognize that.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:08.300
If you squint - and stand really far away...
NIKO: Those eyes - [unint.] Sam's eyes -

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:09.900
Oh that's Jake!
*laughing*

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.920
(Yeah I see it!)
SAM: That makes sense!

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:14.300
It kinda looks like Luigi a little bit.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.040
Yeah I can see Jake for sure.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.240
I like those lips.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.660
Yeah, those freakin' - BAM!
SAM: *popping noise*

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:22.920
- Gabe.
What?! That's not Gabe!

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:25.060
NIKO: That's so obviously not Gabe.
CLINT: That's Niko!

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:29.200
SAM: This looks like that - like, the Beatles' Yellow Submarine style-like art.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.220
CLINT: This is my favorite one. Christian -

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:33.760
*laughing*

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.060
CHRISTIAN: Dude, that's totally me!

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:36.520
That's my favorite one.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:37.700
Those big eyes -

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:39.380
And the hat!
WREN: Dude, that hat -

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.860
Oh my god, that looks so good!

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:44.800
That's Nick.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:47.220
*laughter*
WREN: Oh whoa!

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.480
NIKO: - lookin' like Picasso over here.

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:51.280
CLINT: I'm a fan of this one...

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:54.960
*laughing, exclaiming*
WREN: What?!

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.620
SAM: His whole face just slid off.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.060
CARMICHAEL: He's like - he's like, "Ehhhh!"

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:01.780
CLINT: - detached, completely from his body, and his face just like - *grunting sounds*

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.280
That's Carmichael.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:05.560
The biggest lips!

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:07.760
CARMICHAEL: Those ape lips - that ape upper lip.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:09.060
all: Gabe -
(oh wow!)

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:10.700
That's a pretty good Gabe!

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:12.080
(pretty good Gabe!) (it gets better!)

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:13.300
And that's Adrian.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:15.360
*laughing*
Looks like Markiplier.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.960
So we're gonna put all these pictures on our Corridor Digital Instagram,

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:21.760
@corridordigital on Instagram - go take a look!

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:22.940
Tell us which one is your favorite,

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.380
tell us which one is your least favorite and most scary.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:29.160
Let us know if we should use these as our profile pictures -

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.680
maybe on the new banner for the Corridor Crew channel.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:32.980
NICK: Dude - Doby Day!

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:34.520
NIKO: Yeah dude, Doby Day.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:35.700
When is Doby Day?
NICK: I dunno!

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.300
CARMICHAEL: When IS Doby Day?

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.800
NIKO: When IS Doby Day?
CARMICHAEL: When IS D-Day?

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:40.980
Doby Day is the day that Adrian broke his collarbone.

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:43.160
On Doby Day, you have the, umm,

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:46.120
annual... uhh, pickling, in the morning

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.220
for your winter stores - yeah, pickling, where you make pickles,

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:50.500
and - you pickle different things,

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:51.860
Followed up by badminton.

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:54.540
Followed up by - we all just drink water for lunch.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:57.960
Then we all update Creative Cloud. We make them jump to new software versions...

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:00.000
*laughing*

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.080
Then, it's ended with, a rousing game of world Olympic hackysack.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:08.640
CARMICHAEL: And, you have to unplug the Internet.

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:10.940
E-fast?
(E-fast.)

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.120
NIKO: Oh, and we all have to get one thing unplugged from our computer,

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:15.440
and we don't know what it is, and we have to figure out how to fix it.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.260
*laughing*

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:18.460
That's real Doby Day!

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:20.860
NICK: I have to hold the camera.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:25.660
Mmm!

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:28.720
*sucking noises*

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.880
CHRISTIAN: I always feel sour right here.

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:32.360
Real hard.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:34.780
NICK: What's wrong with your face?

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:38.560
CHRISTIAN: That's the logo of the Warheads! Literally the Warhead logo.

